<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A2.SS4" title="In Appendix B Prompts ‣ Can Video Large Multimodal Models Think Like Doubters—or Double-Down:A Study on Defeasible Video Entailment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B.4 </span>Prompts in our Classification Framework</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A2.SS5" title="In Appendix B Prompts ‣ Can Video Large Multimodal Models Think Like Doubters—or Double-Down:A Study on Defeasible Video Entailment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">B.5 </span>Prompts in our Generation Framework</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A3" title="In Can Video Large Multimodal Models Think Like Doubters—or Double-Down:A Study on Defeasible Video Entailment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">C </span>Dataset Comparison</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A4" title="In Can Video Large Multimodal Models Think Like Doubters—or Double-Down:A Study on Defeasible Video Entailment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">D </span>Case Study</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_appendix"><a href="#A5" title="In Can Video Large Multimodal Models Think Like Doubters—or Double-Down:A Study on Defeasible Video Entailment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">E </span>Limitations</span></a></li>
</ol></nav>
