<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Ablation study on the classification task, evaluating the effects of ASR-enhanced descriptions, counterfactual reasoning, and rationale refinement. For each model, its best results in each metric are highlighted in <span id="S7.T5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we introduce Defeasible Video Entailment (DVidE), an extension of the video entailment task that requires dynamically revising inferences based on new updates. To enhance classification performance, we propose the Chain of Counterfactual Thought framework, which leverages counterfactual reasoning, ASR-enhanced Video Content Integration, and Rationale Refinement to reduce inference bias. For generation, we develop a framework that integrates an external ASR tool and LLM to produce coherent, contextually relevant updates aligned with the intended strengthener or weakener goal. Our approach significantly improves performance. Additionally, we introduce the Defeasible Video Entailment benchmark, providing a dataset with strengthener/weakener annotations to support future research.
To address the limitations of traditional automatic metrics, we propose a novel LLM-based evaluation method for the generation task.</p>
</div>
</section>
